[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-31079"] :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}\\ge 5x+6.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\ge 5x+6 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x-6 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-5x-6$ lies above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5x-6 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=6,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/51c7484f806696105dd570684f8b194d3c1b7fc3ea27d85a1a17f53e6f7d0a64.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-5x-6\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -1$ or $x\\ge 6.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [6,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection/afcecb864cc8c922d04a9e800204b2733b9614a907013f921dc2c919fcc8bb19" :answer/id #uuid "6cc53cb3-ac2c-5c40-b16b-a2c433f70813" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\le x\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection/8ebe1ab94735904f6c890cb18de082421b88043077f9fcac5fd1a99fd159235f" :answer/id #uuid "5123fc09-d68f-5a66-9cb5-ab5d772b00a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2<x<3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection/2ca19e1d8842043347d8976df2e8884bd21c16eda0cdfb1b994becc485d4ce12" :answer/id #uuid "9aa83bc8-7a74-540d-88db-e19eaa52bbbd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection/bf298b70c2b8deb94fb475ff9fa4b928a087ec1b0b59731ad9668362f3cfacc3" :answer/id #uuid "9df67623-03d3-57a8-b0d0-37e2b6c1bff5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x\\le -6$ or $x\\ge 2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection/d3290c097f4d8af166a01560b842dbd3113c542cfdc1a651f578adb6757d40c8" :answer/id #uuid "a5e32ab7-f1fa-5556-9c14-764d7b51e7da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\le x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d486a9-0c77-56cb-a5d9-cb60b5077939" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-142314/selection/afcecb864cc8c922d04a9e800204b2733b9614a907013f921dc2c919fcc8bb19" :answer-field/choices ["q-142314/selection/afcecb864cc8c922d04a9e800204b2733b9614a907013f921dc2c919fcc8bb19" "q-142314/selection/8ebe1ab94735904f6c890cb18de082421b88043077f9fcac5fd1a99fd159235f" "q-142314/selection/2ca19e1d8842043347d8976df2e8884bd21c16eda0cdfb1b994becc485d4ce12" "q-142314/selection/bf298b70c2b8deb94fb475ff9fa4b928a087ec1b0b59731ad9668362f3cfacc3" "q-142314/selection/d3290c097f4d8af166a01560b842dbd3113c542cfdc1a651f578adb6757d40c8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-142314" :question/id #uuid "fb1e01eb-14f1-577c-a4b7-0a54f287effc" :question/math-academy-id "q-142314" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x-12\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+x-12\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x+4)(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/eda4704129b905a10e379254dfd6d1ff07d593d7f97bbc6126e9d27bfec2f9f2.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-4\\le x\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-142314/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-142314"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "e69649ce-42f9-5691-923a-d247fdd42a5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7196d3d-50f2-5a3e-855d-aedbdfff5577" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276404/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer-field/choices ["q-276404/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "f93f7865-bb56-5650-a8e1-210b3358e2a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0486b523-ad57-5ead-824b-4856aee7f54b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276404/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-276404/field-2/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "919706fc-13ef-523e-8d75-285c6e670a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "52611d45-624a-5dbc-bf7a-21bde6074b0e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276404/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-276404/field-3/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276404" :question/id #uuid "021dad23-6108-5419-9f6e-96c817c309f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-276404" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $6{x}^{2}+21x\\ge 12$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]\\,⋃\\,[${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x & \\ge 12 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}+21x-12$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+21x-12 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-3x)+(24x-12) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-1)+12(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ (3x+12)(2x-1) & =0 \\\\ 3(x+4)(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-4$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/38c1897ec93625527b48ec689fbd65e9a63056e033fa6a7a0c72473f1188e7ea.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+21x-12\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x\\le -4$ or $x\\ge \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-4]⋃[\\frac{1}{2},\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-276404/field-1" "q-276404/field-2" "q-276404/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276404"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "a7c33c78-a992-5bfb-a4ae-52acbb1074d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6abcce9e-293d-5d3b-b327-abc625edeb44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cede853-9e96-5001-b91f-5676128a5dfe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277263/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-277263/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-277263/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer/id #uuid "440795f7-cc0c-5087-b5cf-93b03ee9b058" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a89272e7-ee3e-587f-85dd-97c82980276d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277263/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0" :answer-field/choices ["q-277263/field-2/f022eff7ecaa4435243255d76a2a932e99db9e71ca2b89b05fafca75800709a0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-3/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "deba747d-4ccd-535e-b601-450eff0af74b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c862efd6-8a65-5491-8dfa-f778d618caa6" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277263/field-3/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-277263/field-3/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277263" :question/id #uuid "dbdb8111-2a4d-5f07-9e95-10b7d4c127c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-277263" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-7x\\le 0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\le x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-7x\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-7x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-7x & =0 \\\\ x(x-7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=7,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/e7f9e5a051acca0be45340695fd6c2ddcb9d47936cc1f713245bd22d33151c97.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the $x$-axis or touches this axis.\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0\\le x\\le 7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-277263/field-1" "q-277263/field-2" "q-277263/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer/id #uuid "efac5182-d12a-5b78-968c-f9aa01f5d7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf0d4c-944a-5cf5-881e-dcbc6b721475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277667/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934" :answer-field/choices ["q-277667/field-1/e7bc415b91e8e2558c763c56ce6657ae30e51a7e3c0c90c1d4cd29cdacdf8934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-2/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" :answer/id #uuid "8b9eb35b-a126-5956-be77-460c5ae3f119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b868b0e9-7ae0-50f6-8243-7053e9a125f2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277667/field-2/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-277667/field-2/2ebc133599183e5fdb5b6248a8ea00bdd0440ff336252ee383591a8699a758ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-3/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "ab6898a8-0c6c-568c-acc9-98203dcb0b47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d0a39f-c6f9-59ba-af71-269f2e474f81" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-277667/field-3/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-277667/field-3/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-277667" :question/id #uuid "76733b46-8281-5054-9373-31b632e8685f" :question/math-academy-id "q-277667" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}-17x>-2{x}^{2}+45$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in (${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,⋃\\,(${{field-3}}$,\\,\\infty )$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-17x & >-2{x}^{2}+45 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=6{x}^{2}-17x-45$ lies **above** the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-17x-45 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-27x)+(10x-45) & =0 \\\\ 3x(2x-9)+5(2x-9) & =0 \\\\ (3x+5)(2x-9) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $x=\\frac{9}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059052/assets/f73c9906e6b65d1ddbda91619c7ffbb77408faa0541e2bc16565e0127d334312.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}-17x-45>0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $x<-\\frac{5}{3}$ or $x>\\frac{9}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{5}{3})⋃(\\frac{9}{2},\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-277667/field-1" "q-277667/field-2" "q-277667/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "530fc010-b15b-5877-8ed6-7fd2f8feb37c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-277667"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
